meta {
  name: Projects
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

docs {
  Public reads, admin-only writes. `image` always comes back as a Cloudinary URL string — the `publicId` behind it never leaves the API.

  Every write (create / update / toggle / delete) fires a background POST to the website's `/api/revalidate` **after** the response is sent, so the site drops its cached project data. It is fire-and-forget: a request here never fails because the website is down, and it is skipped entirely when `WEB_REVALIDATE_URL` / `REVALIDATE_SECRET` are unset.
}
